## FALLACY-v2 Audit

Skeleton deaths are promoted only from actual certificates. S6 has a literal
exact-Q unit ideal in the descended full order chart. S5 has modular units and
timeouts, not a death. S1-S4 and S7 have typed chart obligations, not deaths.

No flag/place/series identification is made. The split detector order is not
identified with an actual split unless a branch chart is supplied. For
`u_s>=2`, the split and unsplit duties are kept separate.

No modular unit is promoted to characteristic zero. The S6 finite-field runs
are screens; the exact-Q guided run supplies the death. S5 modular units are
explicitly left as `MODULAR_ONLY`.

The order-basis systems extract the ideal component in the declared ring and
localize by a displayed `T*(sat)-1` generator. Builder gates verify that the
target `x^k` row exists before subtracting `c*x^k`.

The old sparse order-chart deaths are not used for S5. The corrected full
