+## Split windows for `u_s>=2`
+
+A numerical skeleton is not intrinsically “split” or “unsplit.” It decomposes
+into strict-below split charts and their complementary no-split chart.
+Proposition 6.1 gives the floor `delta*>=1`; the descent of Proposition 6.3 is
+licensed only once every genuine separation in
+
+\[
+1<\delta<v_s/u_s,\qquad \operatorname{den}(\delta)\le u_s
+\]
+
+has been excluded. Equality at the ceiling belongs to the descended top-root
+partition and is not a strict-below split.
+
+The exact census is:
+
+| ID | strict window; denominator bound | candidate orders | face types that survive the exact ODE |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| S1 | `1<delta<9/2`; `den<=2` | `3/2,2,5/2,3,7/2,4` | `delta=4: [1,1]` |
