+### Exact top/terminal-band parametrization
+
+Set `E=G^2-F^3`. From the Jacobian identity and the terminal homogeneous form,
+write
+
+\[
+H=x^3h(z),\qquad \Theta=cx^{13}\theta(z),\qquad z=y/x.
+\]
+
+The exact terminal-band equations reduce to the linear differential identity
+
+\[
+3h\frac{d\theta}{dz}-13\frac{dh}{dz}\theta=h^2,
+\qquad \deg\theta\le13.
+\]
+
+The derivative variable is explicitly `z`; no prime symbol is overloaded as a
+field characteristic. This recurrence exactly parametrizes all 14 theta
+coefficients before the nonlinear lower-band Groebner step.
+
+For `[2]`, the solution is unique:
+
+\[
+\theta={z^2(z-1)^3\over1309}
+\left(59049z^8-334611z^7+780759z^6-954261z^5
++636174z^4-212058z^3+23562z^2+1122z+187\right).
+\]
+
+For `[1,1]`, exact elimination uses only the constant pivots
+
+```text
+-13,-10,-7,-4,-1,2,5,8,11,14,17,20,23,26.
+```
+
+After localizing only `s(s-1)`, its sole compatibility row is, up to the
+already invertible factor `-65(s-1)^4/(8602 s^10)`,
+
+\[
+Q_2(s)Q_6(s)=0,
+\]
+
+where
+
+\[
+Q_2=s^2-s+1,
+\]
+
+\[
+Q_6=11s^6-33s^5+12s^4+31s^3+12s^2-33s+11.
+\]
+
+Both polynomials are squarefree and irreducible over `Q`. Neither is inverted:
+the exhaustive closed cover is `V(Q2) union V(Q6)`. The complete solved
+theta coefficients, denominators, residual coefficient, localization audit,
+and zero residual for `[2]` are in
+`box/g9966n1b2-20260903/top-pin-audit.json`.
+
+This is the transferable part of the K=8,9 method: the exact recurrence pins
+the terminal lower band and cuts the moving-root chart to two algebraic
+components before `guided_gb`. The full 103 original coefficient rows remain
