+# Degree `(99,66)`, N1 closure lane batch 2
+
+Date: 2026-09-04  
+Lane: `g9966-n1-batch2-sol56-20260903`  
+Verdict: **PARTIAL**
+
+## Executive verdict
+
+The requested degree-wide theorem is **not closed in this lane**. Of the six
+named remainder skeletons `S1,S2,S3,S4,S5,S7`, exactly one is now dead:
+
+```text
+S5  DEAD[UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0]
+S1  OPEN[FULL-BASIS-TIMEOUT+SPLIT-JOINT-UNBUILT]
+S2  OPEN[EXACT-SYSTEM-SPECIFIED;JOINT-CHART-UNBUILT]
+S3  OPEN[EXACT-SYSTEM-SPECIFIED;JOINT-CHART-UNBUILT]
+S4  OPEN[FULL-BASIS-EMITTER-TIMEOUT+SPLIT-JOINT-UNBUILT]
+S7  OPEN[EXACT-SYSTEM-SPECIFIED;JOINT-CHART-UNBUILT]
+```
+
+Thus the lane-six result is `1 dead / 5 open`. There is also a material
+correction to the inherited tally. Moh Proposition 6.3(3) makes the descended
+Jacobian exponent
+
+\[
+\ell=v_s-u_s-1,
+\]
+
+not `n'-M2'-2`. The charged S6 computation used `ell=2`, whereas S6 requires
+`ell=8`, so that old certificate cannot be consumed. This lane rebuilt S6 at
+the correct exponent and obtained a fresh exact characteristic-zero unit
+certificate. Consequently the sound tally among the seven non-S8 skeletons is
+
+```text
+S5 + corrected S6 = 2 dead of 7 non-S8 skeletons.
+```
+
+Including the separately banked S8 death, the degree-wide census is `3 dead / 5
+open` out of exactly eight. N1 remains open, and this report makes **no claim**
+of `NO-KELLER-PAIR-(99,66)` or resolution of the published open case.
+
+The machine-verifier output is
+`box/g9966n1b2-20260903/results-summary.json`; its verdict is `PASS`, with
+summary SHA-256
+`49943f9dc15aa2676ead4f2dbec0440f3507b75f9da948ae9c559e7543f2c8d0`.
+
+## Frozen-input custody
+
+Before any mathematical or CAS action, the manifest was generated mechanically
+from the readable lane receipt
+`xmodel/g9966-n1-batch2-sol56-20260903.run.v2`. The driver paired each
+`charged_input_<i>_sha256` with the corresponding
+`charged_input_<i>_basename`, pointed the entries at
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.y07qTi/inputs`, and ran `sha256sum -c`. All 14 entries passed.
+There was no hand transcription of a digest.
+
+The generated manifest is
+`box/g9966n1b2-20260903/charged-inputs.sha256`, SHA-256
+`43140fe6829a30e05a8aa679441ec7038c92de6c3ddb812446f74652b80e9531`.
+The structured replay is
+`box/g9966n1b2-20260903/charged-inputs-check.json`; it records the expected and
+observed digest for every input and has `ok=true`.
+
+All new drivers, emitted systems, logs, controls, and verifier output are under
+`box/g9966n1b2-20260903/`. No ledger, `jc2-lean`, or `ideation-*` file was
+edited.
+
+## Mechanical census and ID matching
+
+The frozen, hash-matched `moh_skeleton_full.py` was imported directly. Running
+
+```text
+census(99, Kmin=2, full=True), filter m=66,
+sort by the charged key (M2,V3,V2)
+```
+
+returns exactly eight rows. The replay is serialized in
+`box/g9966n1b2-20260903/enumeration.json`. Every row has `s=3`,
+`d=(99,33,11,1)`, `M1=-66`, and `M3=97`. In the following table
+`V=(V2,V3)`. The last column is the Proposition 6.3 datum, whether or not its
+use is automatic on the original skeleton.
+
+| ID | `M=(M1,M2,M3)` | `d` | `V=(V2,V3)` | `(u_s,v_s)` | corrected descended datum |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| S1 | `(-66,-22,97)` | `(99,33,11,1)` | `(1,9)` | `(2,9)` | `(18,12; M'=(-12,-4), V2'=1, K'=6, u'=5, ell=6)` |
+| S2 | `(-66,22,97)` | same | `(1,7)` | `(4,7)` | `(36,24; M'=(-24,8), V2'=1, K'=12, u'=11, ell=2)` |
+| S3 | `(-66,22,97)` | same | `(5,7)` | `(4,7)` | `(36,24; M'=(-24,8), V2'=5, K'=12, u'=7, ell=2)` |
+| S4 | `(-66,22,97)` | same | `(1,8)` | `(3,8)` | `(27,18; M'=(-18,6), V2'=1, K'=9, u'=8, ell=4)` |
