+
+## Exact no-split systems
+
+Conditionally on exclusion of all strict-below split leaves, the no-split
+complement is licensed for Proposition 6.3. For every partition
+`lambda |- u'`, define
+
+\[
+h_{\rm top}=y^{V'_2}(y-x)^{\lambda_1}
+\prod_{j\ge2}(y-s_jx)^{\lambda_j},
+\]
+
+and
+
+\[
+\omega=\prod_js_j(s_j-1)\prod_{i<j}(s_i-s_j).
+\]
+
+The exact localized system is over `Q` and contains every coefficient of the
+full h-adic remainder of
+
+\[
+J(Q,P)-c x^\ell,
+\]
+
+together with `T*c*omega-1`. Its complete inventory rules are
+
+```text
+h lower:
+  s<K, r+s<K, 0<=r<=u', -r+delta1*s>=B
+
+coefficient space at deficit j:
+  s<K, r+s<=j*K, -r+delta1*s>=j*B.
+```
+
+No support inferred from a lower bound was silently upgraded to an equality.
+The serialized arrays in `split-unsplit-triage.json` list every `(r,s)` pair,
+every partition, and each partition-specific parameter count.
+
+| ID | corrected `(n',m';M2',V2';ell)` | `(delta1,delta2,B)` | `h`; alpha dims; beta dim | partitions | parameters excluding T | generic rows |
+|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| S1 | `(18,12;-4,1;6)` | `(1/3,-1/3,-4/3)` | `13; 15,25,32; 24` | 7 | `110..114` | 352 |
+| S2 | `(36,24;8,1;2)` | `(7/9,-1/9,-4/9)` | `39; 44,68,73; 67` | 56 | `292..302` | 1558 |
+| S3 | `(36,24;8,5;2)` | `(1/27,-1/9,-16/27)` | `12; 13,24,29; 23` | 15 | `102..108` | 1044 |
+| S4 | `(27,18;6,1;4)` | `(5/4,-1/4,-3/4)` | `28; 33,63,70; 62` | 22 | `257..264` | 981 |
+| S7 | `(36,24;28,8;2)` | `(1/7,-3/7,-4/7)` | `20; 22,30,36; 29` | 5 | `138..141` | 1055 |
+
+The final column is a generic-support prediction until a native builder emits
+and hashes the rows. The distinction matters: only emitted rows with a passed
+target gate are certificate systems.
+
