+## Split windows for `u_s>=2`
+
+A numerical skeleton is not intrinsically “split” or “unsplit.” It decomposes
+into strict-below split charts and their complementary no-split chart.
+Proposition 6.1 gives the floor `delta*>=1`; the descent of Proposition 6.3 is
+licensed only once every genuine separation in
+
+\[
+1<\delta<v_s/u_s,\qquad \operatorname{den}(\delta)\le u_s
+\]
+
+has been excluded. Equality at the ceiling belongs to the descended top-root
+partition and is not a strict-below split.
+
+The exact census is:
+
+| ID | strict window; denominator bound | candidate orders | face types that survive the exact ODE |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| S1 | `1<delta<9/2`; `den<=2` | `3/2,2,5/2,3,7/2,4` | `delta=4: [1,1]` |
+| S2 | `1<delta<7/4`; `den<=4` | `5/4,4/3,3/2,5/3` | `3/2: [2,2],[2,1,1]`; `5/3: [1^4]` |
+| S3 | same as S2 | same | same |
+| S4 | `1<delta<8/3`; `den<=3` | `4/3,3/2,5/3,2,7/3,5/2` | `2: [2,1]`; `5/2: [1^3]` |
+| S7 | `1<delta<7/4`; `den<=4` | `5/4,4/3,3/2,5/3` | same partition/order pattern as S2 |
+
+Thus none of S1,S2,S3,S4,S7 can currently be declared globally split or
+globally unsplit: each has the displayed possible split leaves and a no-split
+complement. The non-surviving candidate orders are excluded at the exact face
+level. The surviving faces are necessary conditions, not Keller pairs and not
+joint-chart solutions.
+
+### Exact face equation and parametrizations
+
+Let
+
+\[
+X=u_s\delta-v_s,\qquad b=9X,\qquad a=WX-1+\delta.
+\]
