+# Degree `(99,66)`, N1 closure lane batch 2
+
+Date: 2026-09-04  
+Lane: `g9966-n1-batch2-sol56-20260903`  
+Verdict: **PARTIAL**
+
+## Executive verdict
+
+The requested degree-wide theorem is **not closed in this lane**. Of the six
+named remainder skeletons `S1,S2,S3,S4,S5,S7`, exactly one is now dead:
+
+```text
+S5  DEAD[UNIT_IDEAL_CHAR0]
+S1  OPEN[FULL-BASIS-TIMEOUT+SPLIT-JOINT-UNBUILT]
+S2  OPEN[EXACT-SYSTEM-SPECIFIED;JOINT-CHART-UNBUILT]
+S3  OPEN[EXACT-SYSTEM-SPECIFIED;JOINT-CHART-UNBUILT]
+S4  OPEN[FULL-BASIS-EMITTER-TIMEOUT+SPLIT-JOINT-UNBUILT]
+S7  OPEN[EXACT-SYSTEM-SPECIFIED;JOINT-CHART-UNBUILT]
+```
+
+Thus the lane-six result is `1 dead / 5 open`. There is also a material
+correction to the inherited tally. Moh Proposition 6.3(3) makes the descended
+Jacobian exponent
+
+\[
+\ell=v_s-u_s-1,
+\]
+
+not `n'-M2'-2`. The charged S6 computation used `ell=2`, whereas S6 requires
+`ell=8`, so that old certificate cannot be consumed. This lane rebuilt S6 at
+the correct exponent and obtained a fresh exact characteristic-zero unit
+certificate. Consequently the sound tally among the seven non-S8 skeletons is
+
+```text
+S5 + corrected S6 = 2 dead of 7 non-S8 skeletons.
+```
+
+Including the separately banked S8 death, the degree-wide census is `3 dead / 5
+open` out of exactly eight. N1 remains open, and this report makes **no claim**
+of `NO-KELLER-PAIR-(99,66)` or resolution of the published open case.
+
+The machine-verifier output is
+`box/g9966n1b2-20260903/results-summary.json`; its verdict is `PASS`, with
+summary SHA-256
+`9223f3a2cb073d347ef847af5507f0fc61dbe1829006ded59482d44951a20de1`.
+
+## Frozen-input custody
