+
+## Split windows for `u_s>=2`
+
+A numerical skeleton is not intrinsically “split” or “unsplit.” It decomposes
+into strict-below split charts and their complementary no-split chart.
+Proposition 6.1 gives the floor `delta*>=1`; the descent of Proposition 6.3 is
+licensed only once every genuine separation in
+
+\[
+1<\delta<v_s/u_s,\qquad \operatorname{den}(\delta)\le u_s
+\]
+
+has been excluded. Equality at the ceiling belongs to the descended top-root
+partition and is not a strict-below split.
+
+The exact census is:
+
+| ID | strict window; denominator bound | candidate orders | face types that survive the exact ODE |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| S1 | `1<delta<9/2`; `den<=2` | `3/2,2,5/2,3,7/2,4` | `delta=4: [1,1]` |
+| S2 | `1<delta<7/4`; `den<=4` | `5/4,4/3,3/2,5/3` | `3/2: [2,2],[2,1,1]`; `5/3: [1^4]` |
+| S3 | same as S2 | same | same |
+| S4 | `1<delta<8/3`; `den<=3` | `4/3,3/2,5/3,2,7/3,5/2` | `2: [2,1]`; `5/2: [1^3]` |
+| S7 | `1<delta<7/4`; `den<=4` | `5/4,4/3,3/2,5/3` | same partition/order pattern as S2 |
+
+Thus none of S1,S2,S3,S4,S7 can currently be declared globally split or
+globally unsplit: each has the displayed possible split leaves and a no-split
+complement. The non-surviving candidate orders are excluded at the exact face
+level. The surviving faces are necessary conditions, not Keller pairs and not
+joint-chart solutions.
+
+### Exact face equation and parametrizations
+
+Let
+
+\[
+X=u_s\delta-v_s,\qquad b=9X,\qquad a=WX-1+\delta.
+\]
+
+The exact face identity checked in every displayed chart is
+
+\[
+9a\,q\,{dp\over dz}-b\,p\,{dq\over dz}
+=9(v_s-u_s)p^{W+1}.
+\]
+
+Every residual is exactly zero over `Q`. Antiderivatives below have zero
+constant term.
+
+For S1, `W=31`, `deg p=2`, `deg q=63`, and the sole survivor is
+
+\[
+\delta=4,\quad p=z(z-c),\quad
+q=p^{28}\left(C+7\int p^3dz\right),\quad c\ne0.
+\]
+
+For S2 and S3, `W=23`, `deg p=4`, `deg q=93`:
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+\delta=3/2,\ [2,2]:\quad
+&p=(z^2-c)^2,\\
+&q=(z^2-c)^{45}(C+z^3-3cz);\\
+\delta=3/2,\ [2,1,1]:\quad
+&p=z^2(z^2-c),\\
+&q=z^{45}(z^2-c)^{24};\\
+\delta=5/3,\ [1^4]:\quad
+&p=z(z^3-c),\\
+&q=p^{21}(C+z^9-3cz^6+3c^2z^3).
+\end{aligned}
+\]
+
+For S4, `W=23`, `deg p=3`, `deg q=70`:
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+\delta=2,\ [2,1]:\quad
+&p=z^2(z+3a),\\
+&q=z^{45}(z+3a)^{24}(z-2a),\quad a\ne0;\\
+\delta=5/2,\ [1^3]:\quad
+&p=z(z^2-c),\\
+&q=p^{20}\left(C+10\int p^3dz\right),\quad c\ne0,
+\end{aligned}
+\]
+
+with
+
+\[
+10\int p^3dz=z^{10}-{15\over4}cz^8+5c^2z^6-{5\over2}c^3z^4.
+\]
+
+For S7, `W=13`, `deg p=4`, `deg q=53`; the S2/S3 shapes apply with
+the exponent replacements `45,24,21 -> 25,14,11`.
+
+After fixing the Jacobian scalar, a chart with `C` has three solver variables
+`(c,C,T)` and a chart without it has `(c,T)`, with `T*c-1` (or `T*a-1`).
+These small numbers describe only the exact face parametrization. They do not
+include the major-root coefficients, effective transformations, or full
+Jacobian system.
+
+The full joint starting boxes demonstrate the remaining formation cost:
+
+| ID | F box | G box | T2 box | F/G coefficients after two corner pins |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| S1 | `(54,12)` | `(81,18)` | `(126,28)` | 2271 |
+| S2 | `(42,24)` | `(63,36)` | `(70,40)` | 3441 |
+| S3 | `(42,24)` | `(63,36)` | `(70,40)` | 3441 |
+| S4 | `(48,18)` | `(72,27)` | `(80,30)` | 2973 |
+| S7 | `(42,24)` | `(63,36)` | `(35,20)` | 3441 |
+
+The complete major-incidence, effective `T2/T3`, and Jacobian coupling was not
+formed within the lane budget. Every surviving split leaf is therefore typed
+`OPEN[SPLIT-JOINT-UNBUILT]`.
+
+## Exact no-split systems
+
+Conditionally on exclusion of all strict-below split leaves, the no-split
+complement is licensed for Proposition 6.3. For every partition
+`lambda |- u'`, define
+
+\[
+h_{\rm top}=y^{V'_2}(y-x)^{\lambda_1}
+\prod_{j\ge2}(y-s_jx)^{\lambda_j},
+\]
+
+and
+
+\[
+\omega=\prod_js_j(s_j-1)\prod_{i<j}(s_i-s_j).
+\]
+
+The exact localized system is over `Q` and contains every coefficient of the
+full h-adic remainder of
+
+\[
+J(Q,P)-c x^\ell,
+\]
+
+together with `T*c*omega-1`. Its complete inventory rules are
+
+```text
+h lower:
+  s<K, r+s<K, 0<=r<=u', -r+delta1*s>=B
+
+coefficient space at deficit j:
+  s<K, r+s<=j*K, -r+delta1*s>=j*B.
+```
+
+No support inferred from a lower bound was silently upgraded to an equality.
+The serialized arrays in `split-unsplit-triage.json` list every `(r,s)` pair,
+every partition, and each partition-specific parameter count.
+
+These full-D1/order-basis systems are necessary over-approximations to the
+Keller locus. Their unit ideal is decisive because even the larger necessary
+locus is empty. A nonunit or positive-dimensional result would not establish a
+Keller pair; it would require an exact point, reconstruction in the original
+chart, and a direct Jacobian test.
+
+| ID | corrected `(n',m';M2',V2';ell)` | `(delta1,delta2,B)` | `h`; alpha dims; beta dim | partitions | parameters excluding T | generic rows |
+|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| S1 | `(18,12;-4,1;6)` | `(1/3,-1/3,-4/3)` | `13; 15,25,32; 24` | 7 | `110..114` | 352 |
+| S2 | `(36,24;8,1;2)` | `(7/9,-1/9,-4/9)` | `39; 44,68,73; 67` | 56 | `292..302` | 1558 |
+| S3 | `(36,24;8,5;2)` | `(1/27,-1/9,-16/27)` | `12; 13,24,29; 23` | 15 | `102..108` | 1044 |
+| S4 | `(27,18;6,1;4)` | `(5/4,-1/4,-3/4)` | `28; 33,63,70; 62` | 22 | `257..264` | 981 |
+| S7 | `(36,24;28,8;2)` | `(1/7,-3/7,-4/7)` | `20; 22,30,36; 29` | 5 | `138..141` | 1055 |
+
+The final column is a generic-support prediction until a native builder emits
+and hashes the rows. The distinction matters: only emitted rows with a passed
+target gate are certificate systems.
+
+### S1 actual build and Groebner frontier
+
+The required smallest/lowest-`u_s` priority was followed. S1 was attempted
+first. Native full systems were emitted for six of its seven partitions:
