+
+## Controls and promotion discipline
+
+The shared control bundle is
+`box/g9966n1b2-20260903/controls/controls-summary.json`, SHA-256
+`e60a9e23cb2f43d4cd3bbbe404312c4109f51cdc6da0c4ebd75d9775e3770490`.
+It is attached to both exact deaths, S5 and corrected S6.
+
+Two distinct nonunit controls survive. The inherited tame-form chart is
+zero-dimensional of vector-space length 2 and has the deliberately varying
+Jacobian marker `J=6*x*mu^2`; it is not called an automorphism. The literal
+genuine tame-automorphism control uses
+
+```text
+(f,g)=(x^2+2*mu*y,x),  J=-2*mu,
+(mu,mu_inv)=(-1/2,-2).
+```
+
+At that exact point it specializes to `(f,g)=(x^2-y,x)`, has `J=1`, and has
+polynomial inverse `(u,v)->(v,v^2-u)`. Both inverse compositions reduce
+symbolically to zero. Its exact-Q ideal is accepted, nonunit,
+zero-dimensional, and has vector-space length 1. The verifier independently
+re-hashes its script/output and checks all map, Jacobian, inverse, normal-form,
+and clean-exit markers. Finally, the accepted Hilbert-hint control returns the
+expected value 3640, while its perturbed hint fails. Thus the workflow preserves
+a real tame automorphism and rejects a deliberately damaged invariant.
+
+FALLACY-v2 is enforced as follows:
+
+- the Rabinowitsch-localized systems are inhomogeneous, so modular unit ideals
+  are screens only;
+- no modular-to-characteristic-zero promotion uses homogeneous properness;
+- every death in this report has a clean exact-Q or exact algebraic-Q unit;
+- the sextic compatibility component is covered by an exact irreducible
+  coefficient field and independently screened factor-by-factor at three
+  primes;
+- timeouts, header-only row files, generic row predictions, and face-only ODE
+  solutions are never promoted;
+- no POSDIM result occurred, so there is no unfulfilled exact-point/Jacobian
+  test;
+- no new exit-price assertion is made, hence no exit-basis declaration is
+  emitted.
+
+The independent verifier re-hashes scripts, standard output, individual guided
+JSON certificates, builders, rows, staged manifests, modular factor covers,
+controls, and timeout records. It also insists on `accepted=true`,
+`timed_out=false`, complete markers, zero normal forms, basis size one, and
+dimension minus one for a promoted unit.
+
