+## Source correction: the descended monomial
+
+Moh 1983, Proposition 6.3(3), printed page 197, states under the radius
+hypothesis that, with `x=gamma` and `y=pi`,
+
+\[
+J_{(\gamma,\pi)}(G,F)
+=-\frac{u_s}{b}\gamma^{v_s-u_s-1}.
+\]
+
+The nonzero scalar is absorbed into the localized coefficient `c`, so every
+order-basis system in this report subtracts `c*x^ell` with
+`ell=v_s-u_s-1`. A source and repository audit found no justification for the
+charged helper's assignment `ell=n'-M2'-2`. The two formulas happen to agree
+for S8 and disagree for S1 through S7:
+
+| ID | charged helper exponent | source-correct exponent |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| S1 | 20 | 6 |
+| S2 | 26 | 2 |
+| S3 | 26 | 2 |
+| S4 | 19 | 4 |
+| S5 | 5 | 8 |
+| S6 | 2 | 8 |
+| S7 | 6 | 2 |
+| S8 | 4 | 4 |
+
+This is why the old S5 timeout and old S6 kill were not reused. All systems
+actually promoted here have a mechanical target gate showing exactly
+`J-c*x^8` for S5/S6. The corrected exponents, slopes, inventories, builder
+specifications, and open-family systems are serialized rather than left as
+prose.
+
+## S5: Proposition 6.3/6.4 descent
+
+For S5, `delta_3=-1`, `u_s=1`, and `v_s=10`. Proposition 6.4 supplies the
+radius hypothesis automatically. Put `theta=y^{-1}` and
+
+\[
+\sigma=\sum_{j<10}a_j\theta^j+\pi\theta^{10},\qquad
+\gamma=\theta.
+\]
+
+Then the transformed polynomials lie in `k[gamma,pi]`, are monic in `pi`, and
+have degrees
+
+\[
+n'=99/11=9,\qquad m'=66/11=6.
+\]
+
+The full descended data are
+
+\[
+M'=(-6,2),\quad d'=(9,3,1),\quad V'_2=1,\quad K'=3,
+\quad u'=K'-V'_2=2,
+\]
+
+and the correct Jacobian target is
+
+\[
+J(G,F)=c\,x^8,\qquad c\ne0.
+\]
+
+The full order-basis formulas give
+
+\[
+(\delta'_1,\delta'_2,B)=(3/2,-3/2,-3/2),
+\qquad \operatorname{wt}(x^r y^s)=-r+\tfrac32s.
+\]
+
+The complete necessary inventory has 5 lower `h` monomials, alpha coefficient
+spaces of dimensions `7,14,19` at deficits `1,2,3`, and a beta space of
+dimension 13 at deficit 2. After the terminal translation gauge this produces:
+
+| top-root partition | variables before Rabinowitsch `T` | coefficient rows | saturation |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| `[2]` | 59 | 103 | `c` |
+| `[1,1]` | 60 | 103 | `c*s*(s-1)` |
+
+The normalized faces are `H=y(y-x)^2` and
+`H=y(y-x)(y-sx)`, respectively. Native Singular extraction completed for both
+partitions. The row digests are
+
+```text
+[2]    469a189ec168e4e4bb2de98c15a2c18b72069492f68209fb9967ed288ecc9d7e
+[1,1]  2ffe372ffdae5811690cd6d47829d4fcf9e51f3b33bef3444c05d49d43a154a2
+```
+
+The verifier checks the native-done marker, builder digest, exact target gate,
+row count and digest, staged-manifest source digest, and the staged union against
+the monolithic generator union. The `[2]` manifest SHA-256 is
+`fd1f9846d0e38a8c8dfbaad1ef79a8a04571cb611c6528ec0fad01397eef1184`;
+the `[1,1]` manifest SHA-256 is
