+## Source correction: the descended monomial
+
+Moh 1983, Proposition 6.3(3), printed page 197, states under the radius
+hypothesis that, with `x=gamma` and `y=pi`,
+
+\[
+J_{(\gamma,\pi)}(G,F)
+=-\frac{u_s}{b}\gamma^{v_s-u_s-1}.
+\]
+
+The nonzero scalar is absorbed into the localized coefficient `c`, so every
+order-basis system in this report subtracts `c*x^ell` with
+`ell=v_s-u_s-1`. A source and repository audit found no justification for the
+charged helper's assignment `ell=n'-M2'-2`. The two formulas happen to agree
+for S8 and disagree for S1 through S7:
+
+| ID | charged helper exponent | source-correct exponent |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| S1 | 20 | 6 |
+| S2 | 26 | 2 |
+| S3 | 26 | 2 |
+| S4 | 19 | 4 |
+| S5 | 5 | 8 |
+| S6 | 2 | 8 |
+| S7 | 6 | 2 |
+| S8 | 4 | 4 |
+
+This is why the old S5 timeout and old S6 kill were not reused. All systems
+actually promoted here have a mechanical target gate showing exactly
+`J-c*x^8` for S5/S6. The corrected exponents, slopes, inventories, builder
+specifications, and open-family systems are serialized rather than left as
+prose.
